*.bak
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
# A Windows agent can leave a real NTFS device-name entry behind when a
# redirect meant for another shell is interpreted literally. It is never
# project content, and Git must not offer it to `git add -A`.
/nul
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.freebuff/
.saipen/recovery/
.saipen/locks/
# Exact quarantined receipt bodies are local source authority, never a Git or
# archive distribution surface. Export-safe state stays under intake/distribution.
.saipen/quarantine/
# T-994: process-local runtime caches must never enter the tree.
.saipen/cache/
# bootstrap/export.* drops its archive in the project root by design
saipen_export_*.tar.gz
saipen_export_*.zip

thoughts/

# Project scratch directory for ad-hoc debugging artifacts. It is not shipped
# documentation or source; the validator's coverage stage and the audit checks
# must never classify a file under it as a released Markdown document.
/_tmp_dbg/

# A subSaipen's kitchen is a sandbox, and saiwiki's holds a CLONE of the
# GitHub wiki -- a nested git repository. `git add -A` turns that into a
# gitlink: a 160000 entry pointing at a commit no clone of this repo can
# fetch, with none of the content. It landed in v7.122.0 exactly that way.
.saipen/extensions/subs/*/kitchen/wiki/

# T-1350: the same rule, one directory over. saipython's `pen/` is the other
# kitchen sandbox -- its own tracked marker says "Clones of target files land
# here (read from the main tree, edited only as copies). Never the originals.
# Scratch" -- and it was missed when the wiki case was ruled on. It had grown
# two nested git repositories and 1534 untracked scratch files, including whole
# copies of this repository's tools/saipen.py and tools/saipen_engine/, all of
# which the whole-project delivery inventory was collecting as real content.
# The marker itself stays tracked, so the directory keeps saying what it is.
.saipen/extensions/subs/*/kitchen/pen/*
!.saipen/extensions/subs/*/kitchen/pen/_gitkeep

# Per-machine agent permissions. Untracked and unshared on purpose: it is
# local trust, not project content, and `git add -A` would otherwise publish
# one machine's allowlist as everyone's.
.claude/settings.local.json
.saipen/extensions/subs/*/kitchen/_gen_*.py
saipen-delivery.zip

# Wave 15 handoff artifact: large roadmap file, not shipped runtime. Keep out of
# root-file-set and coverage checks; validator honours .gitignore.
impl1.md

# Installed launcher bytes are RENDERED at install time from the single source
# owner bootstrap/cli_launcher.py, into <skill>/bin/. The repository copy would
# only ever name the maintainer clone (absolute interpreter + checkout path), so
# it is a generated artifact, never a tracked one.
/bin/

# The top-level research kitchen. Its scratch held 4547 files / 90 MB: per-ticket
# run logs, one-shot probe and mutation-candidate scripts, live-agent
# stdout/stderr, and five whole-repo candidate trees. None of it is protocol,
# runtime, or evidence -- it is what a ticket's build step happened to write --
# and a fresh `git clone` was paying 90 MB to receive it. The CI TEST TREE CLEAN
# gate already declared untracked `.saipen/kitchen/` debris a failure; tracking
# it was the only reason that gate never fired.
#
# The two registry files are project memory and stay tracked, so the directory
# keeps saying what it is.
/.saipen/kitchen/*
!/.saipen/kitchen/cohort_registry.json
!/.saipen/kitchen/digest.md

# saitranslate is a subSaipen, so its kitchen is a sandbox under the same rule
# as `.saipen/extensions/subs/*/kitchen/` above, and its `.translation-cache` is
# a process-local cache under the same rule as `.saipen/cache/` (T-994). Both
# shipped anyway: 2093 files, 20 MB, none of it a translated locale anyone reads
# from the repository. `.prepare-staging/` is the loader's scratch. SUPERSEDED/
# holds packages that lost their race and can never be published.
#
# READY/ and SETTLED/ stay tracked: those are packages still owed a publish.
/.saipen/saitranslate/kitchen/
/.saipen/saitranslate/.translation-cache/
/.saipen/saitranslate/.prepare-staging/
/.saipen/saitranslate/SUPERSEDED/
